UPCOMING EVENTS (1 MINUTE PER PERSON)  {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell announced the annual holiday shoe donation drive in partnership with the Manhattan Beach Unified School District. A donation box will be placed in front of each school from December 10 to December 18, 2025. He also shared the sad news of the passing of former City employee Yuri Boltelho and asked everyone to keep his wife, son, family, and friends in their thoughts and prayers.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced that new furniture will be installed at the library next week, and the facility will be closed to the public from Sunday, December 7 through Tuesday, December 9, 2025. However, library staff will be available on Monday, December 8, and Tuesday, December 9, to provide sidewalk service for hold pickups and other assistance. The library is scheduled to reopen on Wednesday, December 10, 2025. Ms. Sargent also responded to City Council questions.\line\line Judy Castongia, representing Trinity Lutheran Church of Manhattan Beach, invited the community to attend a staged reading of \ldblquote It\rquote s a Wonderful Life\rdblquote  on Saturday, December 13, 2025, at 7:00 PM, and Sunday, December 14, 2025, at 12:00 PM.\line\line City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian provided an update on the City\rquote s Sepulveda Boulevard safety initiatives. In response to recent tragedies, the City has partnered with Caltrans and holds tri-weekly meetings to expedite safety evaluations. Efforts include pedestrian improvements, such as crosswalks and visibility, traffic circulation changes, and public education campaigns. The Police Department has increased enforcement along Sepulveda Boulevard, and staff have met with the Live Like Braun Foundation to support its mission of promoting pedestrian safety. The City Manager also responded to City Council questions.\line\line Mayor Pro Tem Franklin announced that he will serve as the City Council representative for the 33rd Annual Beach Cities Toy Drive, a joint effort between Hermosa Beach and Manhattan Beach, taking place at the Joslyn Community Center on December 20, 2025, beginning at 11:00 AM. He encouraged the community to donate unwrapped toys and welcomed volunteers to participate in the gift-wrapping party.\line\line Councilmember Charelian announced that he served as the Manhattan Beach Little League Commissioner last year and will continue in that role this year. He reminded families to register their children, noting that registration will be open from December 12 through December 31, 2025. He also shared that the Little League parade is returning this year for the first time since the COVID-19 pandemic and expressed his excitement to see the children participate.\line\line\pard Mayor Lesser announced that the next Coffee with the Mayor will be held at Metlox Plaza on Friday, December 5, 2025, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM.\cf2\i0\f1\par
}


